From 846396875d722a2f9a9b6c6a0cbfed61936b4c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:02:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] ipa: simple: awb: Sensor colour temperature axis,
 module calibration

The colour temperature that selects the CCM is estimated with the
generic estimateCCT(), which assumes sRGB primaries for the raw sensor
colours. Add a sensor-specific axis from the tuning file: x =
256 * (log2(gainR / gainB) - ref) mapped to a colour temperature by a
table, linearly in mireds.

Read the module calibration EEPROM ("MTK" layout, format tag 0x010B00FF)
that the sensor driver exposes as /sys/bus/nvmem/devices/<model>-eeprom:
module and golden-sample white balance averages, focus codes and the
module shading table. The white balance gains are brought to the golden
sample (divided by module / golden gains) before the colour temperature
is looked up, so that the CCM and the shading tables, tuned on the golden
module, are chosen for the right light on every unit.

Signed-off-by: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
